  "recipeCuisine": "Malaysia",
  "name": "Fried Hard Boiled Eggs in Hot Red Sauce",
  "text": "Fried Hard Boiled Eggs in Hot Red Sauce\n\nYield: 4\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nIngredients\n\n8 shelled hard boiled eggs,\n\n1 stalk of lemongrass (trimmed quartered and crushed),\n\n2 large tomatoes (skinned, seeded, and chopped to a pulp),\n\n1-2 tsp sugar,\n\n2 tbsp dark soy sauce,\n\n1 lime (juiced),\n\n1 sprig of fresh coriander (coarsely chopped),\n\n1 sprig mint (coarsely chopped).\n\nFor the rempah\n\n4-6 red chilies (seeded and chopped),\n\n4 shallots (chopped),\n\n2 cloves of garlic (chopped),\n\n½ tsp shrimp paste.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Process the rempah into a smooth paste.\n\n2. Deep fry the eggs until golden brown.\n\n3. Put some oil in a wok and fry the rempah until it becomes fragrant.\n\n4. Add the lemongrass, tomatoes, and sugar.\n\n5. Cook for 2-3 minutes until it becomes a thick paste.\n\n6. Reduce the heat.\n\n7. Stir in the soy sauce and lime juice.\n\n8. Add up to 2 tbsp water to thin the sauce then add the eggs and toss until coated.\n\n9. Serve with chopped coriander and mint.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "8 shelled hard boiled eggs,",
    "1 stalk of lemongrass (trimmed quartered and crushed),",
    "2 large tomatoes (skinned, seeded, and chopped to a pulp),",
